timeline.body:
I'd prefer explicit mappings over dynamic templates for the data_stream fields. This guarantees that these do end up in the mapping even when the first document tries to add a bunch of fields to that the field limit is hit.

I think we can just add this directly to logs-mappings which already adds the data_stream.type field. Additionally, we shouldn't map with a nested `properties` but with a flat mapping so that logs data streams can be used with `subobjects: false`.

```
"data_stream.type": {
  "type": "constant_keyword",
  "value": "logs"
},
"data_stream.dataset": {
  "type": "constant_keyword"
},
"data_stream.namespace": {
  "type": "constant_keyword"
}
```

